<%# decor/app/views/storage_locations/index.html.erb - version 1.0 %>
<%# Session B (Storage Locations feature). %>
<%#
Private, owner-scoped list — @storage_locations is ALWAYS Current.owner's
own records (see storage_locations_controller.rb#index; require_login is
enforced there too, so this view never renders for a logged-out visitor).

No pagination: an owner's own storage-location list is expected to stay
small (a handful of named shelves/boxes/rooms), unlike the sitewide public
Computer/Component/SoftwareItem indexes that need geared_pagination's
"Load more" pattern. Revisit with real pagination if that assumption turns
out wrong for a heavy user.
%>

<div class="px-4 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Storage Locations</h1>
    <%= link_to "Add Storage Location", new_storage_location_path, class: button_classes(style: :primary) %>
  </div>

  <% if @storage_locations.any? %>
    <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded divide-y divide-stone-200">
      <% @storage_locations.each do |storage_location| %>
        <%= render "storage_location", storage_location: storage_location %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <%= empty_state("No storage locations yet.") %>
  <% end %>
</div>
